1
00:00:00,059 --> 00:00:05,061
FinalityDesk compares a transfer with an expected request.

2
00:00:05,147 --> 00:00:11,147
This example uses a public Ethereum USDC transfer. No wallet connects.

3
00:00:13,305 --> 00:00:20,307
The network, transfer and canonical block match. Finality passes separately.

4
00:00:20,362 --> 00:00:25,363
Export stores the request and the RPC observations in a JSON file.

5
00:00:25,381 --> 00:00:30,382
Changing the request by one base unit clears the previous result.

6
00:00:32,322 --> 00:00:39,324
The same successful transaction now fails the requested-amount check.

7
00:00:39,397 --> 00:00:46,400
This labeled synthetic example shows a matching transfer awaiting finality.

8
00:00:46,431 --> 00:00:52,433
A report observes one RPC provider. It does not prove invoice ownership or cash receipt.
